<title>UK: Oliver H1 pretax boosted by property sale.</title>
<headline>Oliver H1 pretax boosted by property sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months ending June 29</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		29.86 earnings     vs 12.45 loss</p>
<p> Pretax		     7.55 profit	  vs 3.15 loss</p>
<p> Turnover		   29.37		  vs 34.48</p>
<p> Operating result	 5.01 loss	    vs 2.36 loss</p>
<p> Disposal		   13.39 profit	 vs 0.04 loss</p>
<p> Interest		   0.83		   vs 0.75</p>
<p> Tax			  nil		    vs nil</p>
<p> Retained		   7.55 profit	  vs 3.15 loss</p>
<p>Note - Clothing firm Oliver Group Plc said it expected further operating losses to be recorded in the 31 weeks to February 1, 1997. It passed on its interim dividend. The property disposal gain largely relates to the sale of its Castle Acres site &quot;at a substantial profit,&quot; Oliver said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
